From 6f3a73b454848b8703374c1a7f2c9f754f234b78 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nipuna H Herath <nipunaherath@hotmail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 14:14:25 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 01/16] inkling2: cut per-token kernels, fuse the router norm,
 strided softcap and conv residual

Generation on an R9700 (gfx1201, ROCm) goes from 31.0 to 37.3 tok/s and pp512
from 825 to 861 on Inkling-2-Mini UD-Q8_K_XL; Vulkan tg from 27.0 to 29.6.

model (inkling2):
- clip as threshold * l2_norm(x, threshold), 3 ops instead of 9
- mix: stack the normalized blocks once per prefix, no repeat for one token
- normalize the four loop messages in one op, share the SWA layer input norm
- skip ggml_cont of views that are already contiguous, one zero-sink tensor
- build_attn (rel): cast the F16 mask to F32 once per graph

CUDA/HIP:
- topk-moe fusion accepts SCALE(s = 1, b = eps) in place of the CLAMP of the
  weight sum (Inkling 2, DeepSeek-V4.1)
- fused softcap reads strided rows (a half of a fused gate_up)
- new fusion SSM_CONV -> RESHAPE -> ADD(residual) -> SCALE

KLD vs the previous build 0.0020 (97.6% same top token), the size of the
build's own batch-1 vs batch-512 difference (0.0017). New test-backend-ops
cases for the router shape, strided softcap and the conv residual fusion.
